Description: static real-time gate for plugin and engine C built on libomxdsp
 omx-rt-gate proves that the real-time code of a plugin or an audio engine
 never allocates, locks, sleeps, does I/O or logs. It compiles each real-time
 source with the project's own flags, reads the compiler's call graph, finds
 the functions a host calls from its audio thread in the plugin's LV2, CLAP,
 PipeWire or JACK tables, and follows every call from there, through
 libomxdsp's own code too. Each finding names the call, its place and the path
 from the entry point. The tables it judges against ship with it: one
 forbidden list, one class table and the thread roles of each ABI, with
 libomxdsp's thread tags and call graphs.
 .
 Its documentation is on openmixer.org.

